// SVD - singular value decomposition A = U*S*V^T of [A] (m x n).
// V: orthonormal eigenvectors of A^T A (eigenvalues high to low)
// U: u_i = A v_i / s_i for s_i > 0, extended to an orthonormal basis of R^m
// Out: [C] = U (m x m), [D] = Sigma (m x n), [E] = V (n x n), ʟSV = singular values
// For exact answers it also shows, in fractions: for each eigenvalue of A^T A the
// unnormalised eigenvectors v and A*v (u = A*v/|A*v|), and the extra u vectors unnormalised.
ClrHome
Disp "SVD OF [A]","WORKING..."
dim([A])→ʟZD
ʟZD(1)→A
ʟZD(2)→G
[A]ᵀ*[A]→[F]
[F]→[J]
prgmZEIG
If Z:Then
Real
Disp "NUMERICAL ERROR:","COMPLEX EIGENVALUES"
Return
End
0*[F]→[E]
G→dim(ʟSV)
0→H
For(U,1,E)
ʟEV(U)→O
[F]-O*identity(G)→[J]
0→S
0→Q
0→W
prgmZRREF
prgmZNULL
[I]→[H]
prgmZGS
// show this eigenspace exactly: unnormalised v's, and A*v (= sigma*u)
ClrHome
Disp "EIGENVALUE OF ATA"
Disp O►Frac
Disp "V VECTORS UNNORMALISED"
Pause [I]►Frac
If O>1ᴇ⁻9:Then
[A]*[I]→[D]
Disp "A*V = SIGMA*U, SO","U = A*V / |A*V|"
Pause [D]►Frac
End
For(J,1,K)
H+1→H
√(max(0,O))→ʟSV(H)
For(I,1,G)
[G](I,J)→[E](I,H)
End
End
End
// rank = number of non-zero singular values
0→U
For(I,1,G)
If ʟSV(I)>1ᴇ⁻6*max(1,ʟSV(1))
U+1→U
End
{A,G}→dim([D])
Fill(0,[D])
For(I,1,min(A,G))
ʟSV(I)→[D](I,I)
End
If U=0:Then
identity(A)→[C]
Else
[A]*[E]→[H]
For(J,1,U)
For(I,1,A)
[H](I,J)/ʟSV(J)→[H](I,J)
End
End
{A,U}→dim([H])
augment([H],identity(A))→[H]
prgmZGS
[G]→[C]
{A,A}→dim([C])
If U<A:Then
ClrHome
Disp "EXTRA U VECTORS:","COLS",U+1,"TO",A,"OF [I] (UNNORMALISED)"
Pause [I]►Frac
End
End
ClrHome
Disp "SINGULAR VALUES","(SQRT OF EIG OF ATA)"
Pause ʟSV
Disp "SQUARED"
Pause (ʟSV²)►Frac
ClrHome
Disp "A = U*S*V^T","U = [C]"
Pause [C]
ClrHome
Disp "SIGMA = [D]"
Pause [D]
ClrHome
Disp "V = [E]"
Pause [E]
